<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head><%- include('../../partials/head', { title: 'Import questions' }) %></head>
<body>
  <div class="flex min-h-screen">
    <%- include('../../partials/sidebar', { active: 'questions' }) %>
    <main class="flex-1 p-8 max-w-2xl">
      <a href="/admin/questions" class="text-sm text-slate-500 hover:text-slate-700">← Back to questions</a>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mt-2 mb-1">📥 Import questions from JSON</h1>
      <p class="text-slate-500 text-sm mb-6">Upload a JSON file matching the schema below. You'll review every question before anything is saved.</p>

      <% if (error) { %>
        <div class="alert-error mb-5">
          <span>⚠️</span>
          <span><%= error %></span>
        </div>
      <% } %>

      <div class="card p-6 mb-6">
        <label class="field-label">Expected JSON schema</label>
        <pre class="rounded-lg bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 text-xs p-4 overflow-x-auto">{
  "questions": [
    {
      "category": "movies",
      "type": "text",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "label": "Guess the movie",
      "prompt": "This 1994 film follows two mob hitmen...",
      "instruct_text": "",
      "media_placeholder": "",
      "media_duration": "",
      "emojis": "",
      "options": ["Pulp Fiction", "Reservoir Dogs", "Kill Bill", "Jackie Brown"],
      "correct_index": 0,
      "clues": [],
      "timer_seconds": 20
    }
  ]
}</pre>
        <ul class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-3 space-y-1 list-disc list-inside">
          <li><code>category</code> should match an existing category's slug (case-insensitive); a numeric <code>category_id</code> is also accepted.</li>
          <li><code>type</code> is one of: image, audio, video, text, emoji, progressive.</li>
          <li><code>options</code> needs exactly 4 entries; <code>correct_index</code> is 0-3.</li>
          <li><code>clues</code> (up to 6) only apply to the <code>progressive</code> type.</li>
          <li>Everything except category/type/label/prompt/options/correct_index is optional.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="card p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-1.5">
          <label class="field-label mb-0">🤖 AI prompt <span class="font-normal text-slate-400">(copy into ChatGPT, Claude, etc.)</span></label>
          <button type="button" id="copy-prompt-btn" class="btn-secondary py-1.5 px-3 text-xs">Copy prompt</button>
        </div>
        <pre id="ai-prompt-block" class="rounded-lg bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 text-xs p-4 overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre-wrap">You are generating quiz questions for a trivia app, to be bulk-imported via JSON.

Generate [NUMBER] quiz questions about "[TOPIC]".

Output ONLY a single valid JSON object matching the shape below — no markdown code fences, no commentary before or after it, no trailing commas, no comments. It must be parseable by a strict JSON.parse().

{
  "questions": [
    {
      "category": "&lt;one of: <%= categories.map(c => c.key_slug).join(', ') %>&gt;",
      "type": "&lt;one of: image, audio, video, text, emoji, progressive&gt;",
      "difficulty": "&lt;one of: easy, medium, hard, extreme&gt;",
      "label": "&lt;short ALL-CAPS section title, e.g. 'READ &amp; ANSWER', max 64 characters&gt;",
      "prompt": "&lt;the question text shown to the player, max 255 characters&gt;",
      "instruct_text": "&lt;optional tone/style hint for text-to-speech narration, or an empty string&gt;",
      "media_placeholder": "&lt;only when type is 'image': a short description of the image to show, otherwise an empty string&gt;",
      "media_duration": "&lt;only when type is 'audio' or 'video': clip length like '0:12', otherwise an empty string&gt;",
      "emojis": "&lt;only when type is 'emoji': 3-5 emoji that encode the answer, otherwise an empty string&gt;",
      "options": ["&lt;exactly 4 answer choices as strings, only one of which is correct&gt;"],
      "correct_index": &lt;integer 0-3, the index into "options" of the correct answer&gt;,
      "clues": ["&lt;only when type is 'progressive': 3-6 clues ordered from vague to obvious, otherwise an empty array&gt;"],
      "timer_seconds": &lt;integer seconds to answer, or 0 for untimed&gt;
    }
  ]
}

Rules:
- "category" must be exactly one of the slugs listed above (case-insensitive) — do not invent new categories.
- "options" must have EXACTLY 4 entries, all non-empty and plausible, with only one correct.
- "correct_index" must point at the correct entry in "options" (0-based).
- Only fill "clues" when "type" is "progressive"; leave it as [] otherwise.
- Only fill "media_placeholder" when "type" is "image"; only fill "media_duration" when "type" is "audio" or "video"; only fill "emojis" when "type" is "emoji". Leave the others as empty strings "".
- Vary "difficulty" and "type" across the batch instead of repeating the same ones for every question.
- Do not repeat the same question, phrasing, or answer twice within the batch.
- Return raw JSON only — no ```json fences, no leading/trailing text.</pre>
      </div>

      <div class="card p-6">
        <form method="post" action="/admin/questions/import" class="space-y-5" id="import-form">
          <input type="hidden" name="payload" id="payload-field">
          <div>
            <label class="field-label">JSON file</label>
            <input type="file" accept=".json,application/json" id="json-file-input" required class="field-input">
            <p id="file-error" class="text-xs text-rose-600 mt-1 hidden">Please choose a valid .json file.</p>
          </div>
          <button class="btn-primary" type="submit" id="import-submit">Preview import</button>
        </form>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>

  <script>
    var copyBtn = document.getElementById('copy-prompt-btn');
    copyBtn.addEventListener('click', function () {
      var text = document.getElementById('ai-prompt-block').innerText;
      navigator.clipboard.writeText(text).then(function () {
        var original = copyBtn.textContent;
        copyBtn.textContent = 'Copied!';
        setTimeout(function () { copyBtn.textContent = original; }, 1500);
      });
    });

    var form = document.getElementById('import-form');
    var fileInput = document.getElementById('json-file-input');
    var payloadField = document.getElementById('payload-field');
    var fileError = document.getElementById('file-error');
    var submitBtn = document.getElementById('import-submit');

    form.addEventListener('submit', function (e) {
      var file = fileInput.files[0];
      if (!file) {
        e.preventDefault();
        fileError.classList.remove('hidden');
        return;
      }
      e.preventDefault();
      fileError.classList.add('hidden');
      submitBtn.disabled = true;
      submitBtn.textContent = 'Reading file…';

      var reader = new FileReader();
      reader.onload = function () {
        payloadField.value = reader.result;
        form.submit();
      };
      reader.onerror = function () {
        fileError.textContent = 'Could not read that file.';
        fileError.classList.remove('hidden');
        submitBtn.disabled = false;
        submitBtn.textContent = 'Preview import';
      };
      reader.readAsText(file);
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
